{"name":"Enchanted Meadow","hex":"#b1d4b7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"enchanted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of enchant"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Charmed, delighted, enraptured.","Under the influence of enchantment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enchanted"},{"term":"meadow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A field or pasture; a piece of land either intentionally cultivated with grass or (especially) naturally covered with grass, especially one that is intended to be mown for hay or to be grazed.","Low land covered with coarse grass or rank herbage near rivers and in marshy places by the sea."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cultivate with grass in order to produce hay."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/meadow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Enchanted (Taylor Swift song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Enchanted\" is a song written and recorded by the American singer-songwriter Taylor Swift for her third studio album, Speak Now (2010). Produced by Swift and Nathan Chapman, the song is a power ballad combining pop, rock, and country. The production incorporates gentle acoustic guitars and crescendos after each refrain, leading to dynamic electric guitars, a steady drum beat, and a vocal harmony-layered coda. In the lyrics, a narrator is infatuated with someone after meeting them for the first time, and she worries about whether the initial feeling will be reciprocated."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enchanted_(Taylor_Swift_song)"},{"title":"Meadow","blocks":[{"text":"A meadow is an open habitat or field, vegetated by grasses, herbs, and other non-woody plants. Trees or shrubs may sparsely populate meadows, as long as they maintain an open character. Meadows can occur naturally under favourable conditions but are often artificially created from cleared shrub or woodland for the production of hay, fodder or livestock. Meadow habitats as a group are characterized as semi-natural grasslands, meaning that they are largely composed of species native to the region, with only limited human intervention."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Blumenwiese_bei_Obermaiselstein05.jpg/330px-Blumenwiese_bei_Obermaiselstein05.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meadow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Taylor_Swift_24_-_Live_in_Paris_-_2011.jpg/500px-Taylor_Swift_24_-_Live_in_Paris_-_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Taylor_Swift_24_-_Live_in_Paris_-_2011.jpg/1280px-Taylor_Swift_24_-_Live_in_Paris_-_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Taylor_Swift_24_-_Live_in_Paris_-_2011.jpg/500px-Taylor_Swift_24_-_Live_in_Paris_-_2011.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Swift singing \"Enchanted\" on her Speak Now World Tour (pictured in Paris in 2011)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATaylor_Swift_24_-_Live_in_Paris_-_2011.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Bergwiese-Kaernten-2008-Thomas_Huntke.jpg/500px-Bergwiese-Kaernten-2008-Thomas_Huntke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Bergwiese-Kaernten-2008-Thomas_Huntke.jpg/500px-Bergwiese-Kaernten-2008-Thomas_Huntke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Living meadow, Austria","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABergwiese-Kaernten-2008-Thomas_Huntke.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Hay_Meadow_-_geograph.org.uk_-_513892.jpg/